--- a/ab_power_meter_monitor.py
+++ b/ab_power_meter_monitor.py
@@ -10,13 +10,13 @@
 ===============================================================================
  Title          : AB Power Meter Monitor (NRAO / GBO site infrastructure)
  Filename       : ab_power_meter_monitor.py
- Version        : 1.6.2 (Semantic Versioning 2.0.0, MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
+ Version        : 1.6.3 (Semantic Versioning 2.0.0, MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH)
  Author         : William W. Wallace
  Company        : NRAO/GBO
  Email          : wwallace@nrao.edu   (alt: naval.antennas@gmail.com)
  Phone          : +1 (304) 456-2216
  Created        : 2026-05 (first internal release; see git history)
- Modified       : 2026-10-26
+ Modified       : 2026-10-27
  Language       : Python 3.12 (primary, tested); 3.8 - 3.11 supported.
                   The source stays at the Python 3.7 language level, so a
                   3.7.11 host still runs it with requirements-py37.txt pins.
@@ -142,6 +142,25 @@ REFERENCES
 
 REVISION HISTORY
 ----------------
+1.6.3  2026-10-27  Findings of the first real-Windows test (Windows 11, i9).
+                   * GUI crash 0xC06D007F (Visual C++ delay-load "procedure not
+                     found") on the first preview plot was NOT in this program:
+                     Intel oneMKL 2026.1.0, conda-forge's default BLAS for NumPy
+                     on Windows, crashed inside np.dot on that CPU. The Windows
+                     test kit now pins OpenBLAS (libblas=*=*openblas). The
+                     headless monitor never multiplies matrices, so it was
+                     never affected.
+                   * OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS defaults to 1 (BLAS_MAX_THREADS) before
+                     NumPy is imported: OpenBLAS's per-thread buffers showed as
+                     ~3 GB of commit charge; one thread is plenty here.
+                   * An unreachable meter (refused / no route / connect
+                     timeout) has its remaining pages skipped for the poll
+                     (SKIP_PAGES_WHEN_UNREACHABLE): ~3 log lines and one page's
